From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: knapcio <knapcio@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:01:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/14] Decode attention round 2: G6_ATTN_SC2_TR=2,
 G6_ATTN_CTX3, G6_ATTN_SEL2, G6_IDX_GRP (exact, default off); attnk bench vs
 round 1

scores_sc<S,2> (G6_ATTN_SC2_TR=2): round 1's transpose reduction done eagerly (heads in bit-reversed order, each combine
as soon as both of its entries exist): the same combines of the same values -> TR=1 bytes, 128 registers instead of 168 at
S=4. G6_ATTN_SC2=8 builds S=8 with TR=0.
context_pk3 (G6_ATTN_CTX3=1..4, G6_ATTN_CTX3_HG): context_pk with 32-bit KV row indices, per-batch states from warp ballots
(skip / plain fmaf with no test / context_pk's select), 32-bit load registers, D = 256 or 512 dims per CTA: per chain the
same fmaf operands in the same slot order and the same skips -> parts bit-identical. Rows must fit in 32 bits (dispatch).
rank_selected (G6_ATTN_SEL2=8/16/32/64): the decode selector's final sort as a rank by count over CH CTAs per row (nonzero
keys are distinct; -1 past nnz) -> the indices of sort_selected<false>/<true>/sort_selected32.
index_scores_g (G6_IDX_GRP=G): the per-row decode indexer (S2 batched steps) reads each key tile once for up to G rows of
one session; per row index_scores' wmma tiles and epilogue -> scores and ids bit-identical.
Flags unset: the same launches as before. SEL2 and IDX_GRP act in run_body only (prefill and CP paths unchanged).
tests/attnk.cu: timing against BASE = round 1 (SC2=4 TR=1 CTX2=4), bytes against stock (now also the indexer's scores and
ids and the appended index pages), two sessions on disjoint page tables (ATTNK_SESS=2), index-score ties (ATTNK_TIES=1),
probability underflow (ATTNK_QSCALE), every changed node timed.
